│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ brick_layer_cnot_circular                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Key improvements over seed:                                                               │
│                          │ 1. Brick-layer CNOT entanglement (alternating even/odd pairs) instead of linear CZ chain  │
│                          │ - gives full circular connectivity in just 2 sub-layers, meaning information can          │
│                          │ propagate across all qubits faster.                                                       │
│                          │ 2. CNOT gates instead of CZ for potentially better gradient properties with the RY        │
│                          │ rotations.                                                                                │
│                          │ 3. Circular topology (7→0 connection) closes the entanglement ring so no qubit is at a    │
│                          │ "dead end".                                                                               │
│                          │ 4. Structure: RY+RZ (full single-qubit rotation) → brick-CNOT → RY (post-entanglement     │
│                          │ rotation). The final RY after entanglement (instead of RZ in seed) provides a different   │
│                          │ rotation axis, improving expressibility since the entangling layer already generates      │
│                          │ Z-type correlations.                                                                      │
│                          │ 5. Same 24 parameters per block as seed, so total param count stays at 144 (6 blocks),    │
│                          │ avoiding overfitting while maximizing expressibility per parameter.                       │
