│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bipartite_tunable_cascade                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This approach takes inspiration from the highly efficient collective parameter sharing of │
│                          │ previous programs but introduces a fundamentally new paradigm: Bipartite Tunable          │
│                          │ Entanglement.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insights:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. **Parameterized Two-Qubit Gates**: Unlike previous iterations that used static `CZ` or │
│                          │ `CNOT` gates, this algorithm uses `CRY` and `CRZ` gates. This grants the optimizer        │
│                          │ dynamic control over entanglement generation, allowing the circuit to actively tune or    │
│                          │ suppress correlations depending on the dataset features rather than forcing an arbitrary  │
│                          │ fixed entangling geometry.                                                                │
│                          │ 2. **Bipartite Parameter Sharing**: Instead of completely uniform parameter sharing       │
│                          │ (which forces identical behavior on all wires) or zero parameter sharing (which leads to  │
│                          │ overfitting and gradient vanishing), this design groups the qubits into two subsets by    │
│                          │ parity (even/odd). This bipartite symmetry creates two interleaved functional roles,      │
│                          │ providing a superior trade-off between representational capacity and trainability.        │
│                          │ 3. **Cross-Topology**: It implements a 1D alternating entangling ring (`CRY` from         │
│                          │ Even->Odd, then Odd->Even) augmented by long-range distance-4 connections (`CRZ`). This   │
│                          │ specific topology ensures all subsets of the dataset features are rapidly mixed while     │
│                          │ avoiding the deep circuits characteristic of all-to-all connectivity.                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
